Add public method to reset the URI generation cache.

UriBuilder (SingletonInterface) caches generated URIs keyed by
route+parameters+referenceType. The cache key is computed before
the CSRF token is injected, so cached URIs carry stale tokens from
previous sessions. Under PHP-FPM this dies with the process; under
long-running runtimes it causes token validation failures and
redirect loops.

Add a public resetGeneratedCache() method so the per-request URI
cache can be cleared without reaching into protected state.

--- a/Classes/Routing/UriBuilder.php
+++ b/Classes/Routing/UriBuilder.php
@@ -75,6 +75,17 @@
     ) {}
 
     /**
+     * Clears the in-memory URI generation cache.
+     *
+     * Useful for long-running PHP runtimes where the singleton instance
+     * persists across requests and cached URIs may carry stale CSRF tokens.
+     */
+    public function resetGeneratedCache(): void
+    {
+        $this->generated = [];
+    }
+
+    /**
      * @internal
      */
     public function setRequestContext(RequestContext $requestContext): void
